{ Hello everyone! Today I am going to show you my repertoire against the Caro-Kann! The Caro-Kann is an increasingly popular opening, so you will face it a lot in your games.

Abbreviation I will use some in my study:
IQP=Isolated Queen's Pawn

READ THIS

This study will be completely different from my other studies. Instead of giving you one repertoire, I will give you three choices. Your style and preferences are what matters! So, you can decide to play all three repertoires, taking turns, or sticking to one repertoire. However, that does not mean you should only look at one part of my study. Instead, the other repertoires you don't look at could be very helpful at understanding the positions you encounter in the repertoire you chose.

This Study was made for beginner-intermediate players, circa 1200-1900. }
1. e4 { In this study, I will look at three different repertoires from which you can choose. I will call them the "Open," "Half-Open," and "IQP" repertoires. } 1... c6 { With this move, black prepares d5 while also keeping the light-squared-bishop free to go to f5. The main downside of this move is that c5 takes an extra tempo to play. We will not go into this in detail, but then you know why some moves are played.
Here, we will look at our 3 possible repertoires. The "Open" repertoire will start with d4, the "Half-Open" repertoire will start with Nf3, and the "IQP" repertoire will start with c4.
You will also need to choose on the basis of how much time you have. If you are a beginning player or just want to keep it simple, I recommend choosing Repertoire 1 or 2, though Repertoire 2 is pretty complex for beginning players. If you have a lot of time to study and good at attacking, Repertoire 3 will be good for you.
Join our team for more studies! lichess.org/team/study-creators--friends } { [%cal Gc2c4,Gd2d4,Gg1f3,Gd7d5,Gc8f5,Rc7c6,Rc6c5] } 2. d4 { "Open" repertoire } { [%cal Gc2c3] } (2. d4 { "Open" repertoire } { [%cal Gc2c3] }) (2. Nf3 { "Half-Open" repertoire } { [%cal Gb1c3] }) (2. c4 { "IQP" repertoire } { [%cal Gc4d5,Ge4d5] }) *


[Event "Crush the Caro-Kann! White Repertoire: Repertoire 1: \"Open\""]
[Date "2024.01.30"]
