3... d4? { Surprisingly, a mistake. Played around 10% of the time, mostly at the level 14-1700. So you will now learn how to refute this move! } 4. Ne2 { Obvious. Black now has to defend his pawn, and there's only 1 way of doing that. } { [%csl Rd4][%cal Re2d4,Rf3d4] } 4... c5 5. c3! { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rc3d4] } 5... Nc6 (5... dxc3 6. Nxc3 { Usually, our next move is d4. } { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rd2d4] }) (5... d3? 6. Nf4! { The pawn has to be defended... } { [%csl Rd3][%cal Rf4d3,Rf1d3] } 6... c4? 7. Qa4+ { It's over now. White wins 2 pawns, without compensation for black. } { [%csl Re8,Rc4,Rd3][%cal Ra4e8,Ra4c4,Rf1d3,Rf4d3] }) 6. cxd4 cxd4 (6... Nxd4 7. Nexd4 cxd4 8. Qa4+! { Winning a pawn. } { [%csl Rd4,Re8][%cal Ra4d4,Rf3d4,Ra4e8] }) 7. Qa4 { Simultaneously pinning the knight and attacking the pawn. } { [%csl Re8][%cal Ra4e8] } 7... Bd7 { [%csl Ra4][%cal Rd7a4] } (7... d3 8. Ned4! { [%csl Rc6][%cal Rd4c6,Ra4e8] } 8... Bd7 9. Bxd3 { Same here - we won a pawn, now we should win. } 9... Nxd4 10. Qxd4) (7... e5 8. Nxe5! { We are winning. } { [%csl Rd4,Rc6][%cal Re2d4,Ra4d4,Re5c6,Ra4e8] } 8... Bd7 9. Nxc6! Bxc6 10. Qxd4 Qxd4 11. Nxd4 Bxe4 12. Bb5+ { We should easily win. }) 8. Nexd4! Nxd4 9. Qxd4 { We have simply won a pawn. Now we just complete our development, castle, and we should win easily. } *


