10... Bh5 { The best move according to the computer and the most played one. } 11. d5! { An important in-between move! It would be intuitive to play 11.Bf4 Nxd4 12.Kd2 to not block your own bishop, but it's bad. } { [%csl Rc6][%cal Rd5c6] } 11... Nd4 12. Bf4! Nc2+? { Most obvious and also the most played move, but it's a huge mistake. } (12... e5!! { An absolutely excellent defensive move! } 13. dxe6+ fxe6 14. Rc1 { Black's the one pressing, but we're up an exchange. } 14... Bb4+ 15. Bd2 Bxd2+ 16. Kxd2 Nf6 (16... Nc6 17. b4! { We need to free our knight. } { [%csl Rb5,Rc7][%cal Rb4b5,Ra8c7] } 17... Nf6 18. Nc7! Kxc7 19. b5 { We have a nice position. }) 17. Nc7 { We should be able to convert this. } 17... a6 18. Bd3 Nc6 19. Rxc6! { We end up a pawn. }) 13. Kd2 Nxa1 14. Bb5+!! { All of a sudden there are problems! } { [%csl Rd7][%cal Rb5d7] } 14... Kd8 (14... Kc8?? { Mate in 7! } 15. Rc1+! Kd8 (15... Nc2 16. Rxc2+ Kd8 17. Bc7+ Kc8 18. Nb6+! axb6 19. Bxb6+ Kb8 20. Bd7 { It's over. } { [%csl Rc8][%cal Rc2c8] }) 16. Bc7+ Kc8 17. Nb6+! axb6 18. Bxb6+ Kb8 19. Bd7 { The only thing black can do is delay the mate. } { [%csl Rc8][%cal Rc1c8] }) 15. Bc7+ Kc8 16. Rc1 { Big threats. At the moment black is up a knight, but we have sufficient compensation. } { [%csl Rc8][%cal Rc1c8] } 16... Nf6 { The best defensive try. } (16... b6?? 17. Bxb6+! Kb8 (17... Kb7 18. Rc7+ Kxa8 19. Bxa7 { [%csl Rc6,Ra8][%cal Rb5c6,Rc6a8] } 19... Nb3+ 20. axb3 e6 21. Bc6#) 18. Bc7+ Kc8 (18... Kb7 19. Be5! { There's nothing that can be done. } { [%csl Rc7][%cal Re5c7,Rc1c7] } 19... h6 20. Rc7+ Kb8 (20... Kxa8 21. Rc8+ Kb7 22. Rb8#! { [%csl Rb7][%cal Rb8b7] }) 21. Rc6+ Kb7 22. Ba6+ Kxa8 23. Rc8#) (18... Kxa8 19. Bc6#) 19. Ba5+ Kb8 (19... Kb7 20. Rc7+ Kb8 (20... Kxa8 21. Bc6+ Kb8 22. Rb7+ Kc8 (22... Ka8 23. Rb5#) 23. Rxa7 { Next move is Ra8#. } { [%csl Ra8][%cal Ra7a8] }) 21. Ba6! { A very simple threat of Rc8#. } { [%csl Rc8][%cal Rc7c8] } 21... Bg4 { [%cal Gg4c8] } 22. Rb7+ Kc8 (22... Kxa8 23. Bc7 { It's over. } { [%csl Rb8][%cal Rb7b8] }) 23. Rxe7+ Kb8 24. Re8+ Bc8 25. Rxc8#) 20. Nc7! { Black can do nothing to avoid being mated! } 20... a6 21. Nxa6+ Ka8 22. Rc8+ Ka7 23. Rc7+ Ka8 24. Bc6#) 17. Be5+ Kd8 18. Rc7! { Black's busted. Your attacking and tactical skills should do the rest. } { [%csl Rb7][%cal Rc7b7] } *


