4... Nf6 { The main line. } 5. d4 Nxd5 6. Nc3 { We just enter the mainlines of the Panov. } 6... e6 (6... Nc6 7. Nf3 Bg4 8. Qb3! { [%csl Rb7,Rd5][%cal Rb3b7,Rb3d5,Rc3d5] } 8... Bxf3 9. gxf3 e6 10. Qxb7 Nxd4 11. Bb5+ Nxb5 12. Qc6+! { An intermediate move to force the black king to e7! } 12... Ke7 13. Qxb5 { We have a great position. }) 7. Bd3 Bb4 (7... Nc6 8. Nf3 Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. Re1) (7... Be7 8. Nf3 O-O 9. O-O Nc6 10. Re1 { These two are the same position, we have a slight edge. Our knight will jump into e5 soon, with a potential rook-lift. With a bishop on c4, there are sacrifices on f7 too. Sometimes a Greek gift sacrifice is also available, let's make some careless moves for black. } { [%csl Re5,Bg3,Bh3,Yf7,Yc4,Rh7][%cal Rf3e5,Be1e3,Be3h3,Rg3g8,Rh3h8,Ye5f7,Yd3c4,Yc4f7,Rd3h7] } 10... Bd7?! 11. Ne5 Re8? 12. Bxh7+! Kxh7 13. Qh5+ Kg8 14. Qxf7+ Kh8 15. Re4 { [%csl Rg6,Rg4,Rh4][%cal Re5g6,Re4g4,Re4h4] } 15... Rc8?! 16. Rg4 { [%csl Rg7][%cal Rg4g7,Rf7g7] } 16... Bf6 17. Bh6! { Black can only delay the mate. } { [%csl Rg7][%cal Rh6g7] } 17... Rg8 18. Qh5! { [%csl Rh8][%cal Rh5h8] } 18... g6 { [%csl Rh5][%cal Rg6h5] } 19. Bg7+ { Double check is important. } { [%csl Rh8][%cal Rg7h8,Rh5h8] } 19... Kxg7 20. Qxg6+ Kf8 21. Qf7#) 8. Ne2 { We will play a simple, strategic middlegame. We play a3 to kick the bishop away, castle kingside, Re1, and Bf4 to play aggressively. } { [%csl Gc3,Gd4,Ga3,Gf4][%cal Ge2c3,Ge2d4,Ga2a3,Gh1e1,Gc1f4] } *


